ImageViewer patch (docs/PLAN.md section 15, D-57, D-93): filtered layers drawn only within reach of the view
Library: resvg 0.48.1
Fixes: none (speed: a filtered layer cost its whole filter region, linebender/resvg#790 and #1192)
Upstream: none yet: to be proposed to linebender/resvg, linked to #1192 (ours)
Remove when: a resvg release draws a filtered layer only within reach of the canvas, or this patch no longer applies

resvg drew every filtered group over its whole filter region at the scale asked, however little of it
the canvas shows: a part of the canvas cost as much as the whole, and a zoomed-in view its whole area
at that zoom. Here a layer is drawn only within reach of the visible area (render::Context::visible):
for a filtered group, the reach of its filters (filter::reach(): the box blur's exact width, offsets,
morphology, displacement, convolution, lighting); a filter whose result may depend on its whole region
(feTile, feImage, stitched feTurbulence) keeps its whole region, as before. Groups and layers outside
the visible area are not drawn: tiny-skia 0.12 drew a one-row pixmap placed just above the canvas onto
the canvas's first row. A primitive's subregion is cleared within its result's pixels wherever it lies
(it may lie partly or wholly outside a layer drawn in part). The pixels are those of the whole region
but for anti-aliased edges, whose coverage may move by a rounding step when a layer starts elsewhere
(tiny-skia's, as for a shape drawn on a canvas that starts elsewhere; lighting and convolution, which
read an edge's slope, enlarge that step): 3 of resvg's 1,730 reference tests differ there.

